= Academic publishing =

== Overview ==
'''Academic publishing''' is the set of processes and institutions used to prepare, evaluate, produce, register, distribute, and preserve scholarly works.

It includes journals, books, conference proceedings, repositories, editorial systems, publishers, learned societies, and digital publication infrastructure. Peer review is common but is not identical to publishing itself.

Publication status records that a work has entered a dissemination process or venue; it does not by itself establish the correctness of every claim.

== Boundaries ==
* academic publishing ≠ peer review
* publication ≠ correctness
* publisher ≠ owner of scientific truth

